      "writtenOn": "2017-10-23T08:21:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Vincent:\nIn CL 284036, the uart driver set the WKAEDG bit which belongs to RX pin before selecting to GPIO to make sure ec can wake-up from deep idle if there\u0027s a falling edge on RX pin. The line 65 should be \"SET_BIT(NPCX_WKEDG(1, NPCX_UART_WK_PORT_N), NPCX_UART_WK_BIT);\". Otherwise ec won\u0027t wake-up by the uart received transaction when RX pin is selected to GPIO.",
      "parentUuid": "37543e32_3de644e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "43ce8811b5c8abea09580a9c43f3478832ec23e6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
